From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] map-controller: tripwire node without policy
Signed-off-by: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>

Tripwire: never dereference node policy that was never bound.

cntlr_check_config_diff() walks c->agentlist and reads n->np->is_policy_diff.
np is NULL for any node that reached agentlist without a policy binding:
duplicate AL-MAC mirrors (unreachable via mac_table, so never backfilled by
cntlr_resync_config) and agents with no matching UCI node section. Both crash
the controller with SIGSEGV; procd respawns it, so it presents as a restart
loop rather than a crash.

Confirmed on hardware from a core dump: si_addr=0x2d = offsetof(struct
node_policy, is_policy_diff), faulting at ldrb w0,[x0,#45] with x0=0, right
after ldr x0,[x21,#296] = offsetof(struct node, np).

The guard must sit at the top of the loop body, not inline in the existing
condition: with only CONFIG_DIFF_AGENT_POLICY_CNT set that test is skipped and
np still reaches cntlr_gen_policy_config_req() further down.

This is deliberately NOT a fix. The counter is exported as
map.controller status -> nodes_without_policy and MUST read 0. A non-zero
value means node identity is still created from more than one source and the
real defect is upstream in node creation, not here.

--- a/src/cntlr.h
+++ b/src/cntlr.h
@@ -305,6 +305,10 @@
 	 * prebuilt plugin .so's that dereference struct controller* opaquely. */
 	atimer_t db_checkpoint;	/* periodic WAL checkpoint of mapc.db */
 	mapdb *db;		/* persistence handle (mapc.db); NULL = degraded */
+
+	/* Tripwire: nodes that reached agentlist without a policy binding.
+	 * MUST stay 0 once node identity is single-sourced; appended = ABI-safe. */
+	uint32_t nodes_without_policy;
 };
 
 #define STA_CHANNEL_REPORT_MAX_NUM 32
--- a/src/cntlr.c
+++ b/src/cntlr.c
@@ -1433,6 +1433,21 @@
 			struct netif_radio *r = NULL;
 			int num_radio = 0;
 
+			/* A node must never reach agentlist without a policy binding.
+			 * It happens today for duplicate AL-MAC mirrors (unreachable via
+			 * mac_table, so never backfilled) and for agents with no matching
+			 * UCI node section. Both dereference np below and crash.
+			 *
+			 * This is a tripwire, NOT a fix: the counter is exported in
+			 * map.controller status and MUST read 0. If it does not, node
+			 * identity is still multi-sourced and the real defect is upstream. */
+			if (!n->np) {
+				c->nodes_without_policy++;
+				warn("%s: node " MACFMT " in agentlist without policy - INVARIANT VIOLATED (count=%u)\n",
+				     __func__, MAC2STR(n->almacaddr), c->nodes_without_policy);
+				continue;
+			}
+
 			if ((diff & CONFIG_DIFF_AGENT_POLICY) && !n->np->is_policy_diff)
 				continue;
 
--- a/src/cntlr_commands_impl.c
+++ b/src/cntlr_commands_impl.c
@@ -3332,6 +3332,7 @@
 
 
 	blobmsg_add_u32(bb, "num_nodes", c->num_agents);
+	blobmsg_add_u32(bb, "nodes_without_policy", c->nodes_without_policy);
 	a = blobmsg_open_array(bb, "node");
 	list_for_each_entry(n, &c->agentlist, list) {
 		void *t, *tt;
